                            <comment id="15473801" author="zjffdu" created="Thu, 8 Sep 2016 12:58:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=linchan&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;linchan&quot;&gt;linchan&lt;/a&gt; I notice most of places we use relative path for interpreter setting page. Where do you click the link that does not work for you ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15474533" author="linchan" created="Thu, 8 Sep 2016 17:44:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The way I repro&apos;d this is open a notebook, on the top right corner, there is this gear like icon which links to &quot;interpreter binding&quot;. Click that and a Setting section will show up on top of the notebook. The text will be like:&lt;br/&gt;
Bind interpreter for this note. Click to Bind/Unbind interpreter. Drag and drop to reorder interpreters. &lt;br/&gt;
The first interpreter on the list becomes default. To create/remove interpreters, go to Interpreter menu.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The last &quot;Interpreter&quot; is a link and that link seems to be coded with a starting &quot;/&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
